;
; ---- TG voice allocator + steal engine (library image). Static RE of the
;      slot-choice machinery under TgNoteOn (kn7000_mame/notes/
;      tg-voice-allocator.md). Each of the 128 hw slots has a 0x2C-byte
;      VOICE NODE at 0x500D1278 + slot*0x2C: +0x00/+0x04 class-ring links,
;      +0x08/+0x0C free-ring links, +0x10/+0x14 slot-ring links, +0x18
;      order-list base / +0x1C its class, +0x20 current list-array base,
;      +0x24 its class, +0x26 flags halfword (bit0 free, bit1 fading,
;      bit2 sweep-release, bit7 held), +0x28 NOTE, +0x29 HW SLOT
;      (< 0x40 = TG A else TG B), +0x2A last swept level, +0x2B refade
;      class. List arrays are {+0 cntA?, +1 cntB?, +2 A-active, +3
;      B-active, +4.. class ring heads} (+0/+1 = the array's per-side
;      polyphony QUOTA: allocation past it migrates a donor voice's
;      node to the global array; retire never drops a count below it):
;      per-part arrays are POINTED TO by *(0x500D0C64+part*0x1C)
;      (classes 0..5), global active 0x500D1238 (heads 0x500D123C..),
;      global free/retired 0x500D1258 (its class-6 head 0x500D1274 =
;      first-choice free node). STEAL ORDER = ROM byte lists (0xFF-end,
;      bit7 = global ring, else the part's own ring) selected by the
;      pool-descriptor table 0x485879D8 + pool*8 {order-list ptr, +4
;      ring-entry class, +5 refade class}: pool 0 -> 0x486D3844 (cls
;      0/3) [86 85 06 05 84 83 82 04 03
;      02 81 80 01 00], pool 1 -> 0x486D3853 (same minus trailing 00),
;      pools 2..5/8+ -> 0x486D3861 (minus 81 80 01 00), pools 6/7 ->
;      0x486D386C [86 85 06 05 84 83 82 04]: retired (6) first, then
;      releasing (5..2), then held (1,0) -- global before own-part at
;      each priority. Pool select bytes: melodic elems = 0x4858710C
;      [0..3]/[4..7], drum kits = 0x48587114, table kits = 0x48587118. --
0x4C012254  TgPartElemLastClear     ; (d0 part, d1 idx) reset the part's per-element last-entry cache: byte 0x50009E48+part*8+idx*2 := 0xFF (and the record word := idx*2)
