; ---- the TG note-path closure set (2026-07-20 static RE): the per-class
;      note-on/key-off programmers under TgNoteOn/TgVoiceSlotService, the
;      voice-list collect/release engine, and the portamento (glide) pair
;      that the earlier notes read as the "pedal-release collection sweep".
;      KEY REINTERPRETATION (code-settled): the 0x500AD5A8+part*0x10C block
;      +0x26..+0x48 is the part's MONO/PORTAMENTO state, not a damper-pedal
;      mark list -- +0x26 = current (top) note, +0x27 = previous note,
;      +0x28/+0x29 = glide tick period/counter, +0x2A/+0x2C = step count/
;      index, +0x30/+0x38 = per-step pitch deltas (SOFT DOUBLES), +0x40/
;      +0x42 = interpolated pitch offset, +0x46 = curve base step. --------
